                <section id="lineProviders" class="section">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12 left-align">
                            <h2 class="dark-text">AI Providers <hr></h2>
                        </div>
                        <!-- end col -->
                    </div>
                    <!-- end row -->
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12">
                            <p>
                                Run the <b>Server Manager</b> and select the menu <srmenu>Configuration->Configure AI...</srmenu> to configure the AI Providers, Tools and Agents.<br /><br />
                                An <strong>AI Provider</strong> is defined with its <code>Type</code>, its <code>Endpoint</code>, an <code>API Key</code>, a <code>Model</code> name and optional generation parameters (temperature, max tokens).<br />
                                Four provider types are supported:
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><b>OpenAI</b>: OpenAI API or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.</li>
                                <li><b>Azure</b>: Azure OpenAI deployments.</li>
                                <li><b>Anthropic</b>: Claude models.</li>
                                <li><b>Ollama</b>: local models running on your own hardware (offline).</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p>
                                The AI configuration is stored in the <i>/Settings/AI</i> Repository sub-folder.
                            </p>
                            <div class="bs-callout bs-callout-warning">
                                Several providers can be configured (<eg>e.g. a hosted model for the report designers, a local model for the analysts</eg>).
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- end col -->
                    </div>
                    <!-- end row -->
                </section>
                <!-- end section -->
                <section id="lineAgents" class="section">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12 left-align">
                            <h2 class="dark-text">The Agents <hr></h2>
                        </div>
                        <!-- end col -->
                    </div>
                    <!-- end row -->
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12">
                            <p>
                                Each agent is dedicated to a role, with its own system prompt and tool set:
                            </p>
                            <table class="table table-striped">
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Agent</th>
                                        <th>For</th>
                                        <th>What it does</th>
                                        <th>Sample prompts</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><b>Report Designer</b></td>
                                        <td>Report authors</td>
                                        <td>Designs and builds reports from natural-language requests: from the metadata model, from a SQL statement or on NoSQL/LINQ sources. Styles the report views.</td>
                                        <td><i>"Create a report showing sales by country with a bar chart"</i>, <i>"What columns are in the Orders table?"</i></td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><b>Data Analyst</b></td>
                                        <td>End users</td>
                                        <td>Answers data questions by running existing reports and exploring data sources <b>read-only</b>.</td>
                                        <td><i>"What were total sales last month?"</i>, <i>"Show me the top 10 customers by revenue"</i></td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><b>Schedule &amp; Output</b></td>
                                        <td>Power users</td>
                                        <td>Configures report delivery and automation: outputs, devices and schedules.</td>
                                        <td><i>"Create an Excel output for this report saved in my Personal folder"</i>, <i>"Email this report every Monday at 8am"</i></td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><b>System Admin</b></td>
                                        <td>Administrators</td>
                                        <td>Handles administration and troubleshooting: event logs, security and activity audit, file management.</td>
                                        <td><i>"Show errors in today's event log"</i>, <i>"Which schedules failed this week?"</i></td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><b>Data Source Manager</b></td>
                                        <td>Data modelers</td>
                                        <td>Manages the data source metadata model: adds tables, columns, enumerated lists and joins, edits or removes metadata, checks which reports are impacted before any change.</td>
                                        <td><i>"Add a Yes/No enumerated list on Orders.Shipped"</i>, <i>"Which reports use Customers.Country?"</i></td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                            <div class="bs-callout bs-callout-info">
                                <ck>Check <a href="~/Sources#lineAI">AI Data Source Manager</a> for the details of the metadata edition</ck>.
                            </div>
                            <p>
                                <strong>Working with the chat panel</strong>
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><b>Follow-up suggestions</b>: when an agent proposes next steps or asks to choose between alternatives, the options are displayed as links: a click sends the suggestion as the next message.</li>
                                <li><b>Any kind of report</b>: the Report Designer learns Seal like a developer. It searches and reads the sample reports, the view templates and the skills (tools <code>seal_search</code> and <code>seal_read</code>, limited to the <code>Knowledge folders</code> of the AI configuration: by default <i>Views</i>, <i>Reports\Samples</i> and <i>Settings\AI\Skills</i>; the data sources, the security, the settings and the logs are never readable), describes the classes of a report (<code>seal_describe_class</code>: XML elements, types, default values, enumerations, code level) and the parameters of the view templates (<code>view_template_list</code>, <code>view_template_get_parameters</code>). It can then write tabs, containers, cards, KPIs, cross-tabs, charts or maps, and modify a saved report with XPath operations (<code>report_patch_xml</code>) instead of rewriting it. The only limit is the <a href="~/Server#lineSecurity_group">Report code level</a>.</li>
                                <li><b>Reports created by an agent</b> are executed once before they are delivered, then their views are rendered as by the <i>SealReportRunner</i>: the agent checks the result (number of rows, execution error, view errors with their file and line) and fixes the report if the test fails. With an Anthropic provider, the agent can also get a picture of the rendered report to check its layout. The filters of the report are created as prompted restrictions by default, so that the user can change their values at execution. The Report Designer agent can also define drop-down lists in the report and add a <a href="~/Reports#lineViews_map">Map view</a>. A drop-down list of the values of a column is generated by Seal from the column (<code>&lt;FromColumnGUID&gt;</code> in the list), without SQL written by the agent: it is available at the <b>Metadata only</b> level.</li>
                                <li><b>Panel state</b>: the state of the panel (open or closed, width) is saved in the user profile, and the last conversation is selected again after a login.</li>
                                <li><b>CSV export</b> of a result shown in the chat uses the CSV separator of the server configuration.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <!-- end col -->
                    </div>
                    <!-- end row -->
                </section>
                <!-- end section -->
                <section id="lineSecurity" class="section">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12 left-align">
                            <h2 class="dark-text">Security <hr></h2>
                        </div>
                        <!-- end col -->
                    </div>
                    <!-- end row -->
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12">
                            <ul>
                                <li>The agents act <b>as the logged-in user</b>: they can only see and edit what the user's <b>Security Groups</b> allow (folder rights, personal folder, source folder <b>Edit</b> right for metadata changes).</li>
                                <li>Action tools are gated behind <b>skills</b> that the agent must explicitly load: reads are cheap, writes are deliberate.</li>
                                <li><b>Destructive operations</b> require an explicit user confirmation, and every metadata write is backed up automatically.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p>
                                <strong>Limits per user</strong>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                The Security Provider script can limit the use of the agents by setting functions on the user during the login. Seal calls them and the script decides where the consumption is counted (<eg>e.g. a table of its database, per user or per customer</eg>), the periods and the values of the limits:
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><code>user.CheckAIChat</code>: called before each message of the chat panel, returns null to send it or the message displayed to refuse it.</li>
                                <li><code>user.GetAICostLimit</code>: returns the cost the user can still spend (in the currency of the costs of the AI provider) or null for no limit. The answer stops when the cost of the exchange reaches it (the last AI call can exceed it). A message is refused if the AI provider of the agent has no cost configured.</li>
                                <li><code>user.OnAIUsage</code>: called after each exchange with the usage (tokens, calls) and its cost.</li>
                                <li><code>user.CheckMcpCall</code>: called with the tool name before each tool call of the MCP server, returns null to execute it or the message sent to the client to refuse it. <code>user.OnMcpCall</code> is called after each call executed.</li>
                                <li>A refusal is audited (types <code>AIChatRefused</code> and <code>AIMcpRefused</code>). If a check function fails, the message or the call is refused.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <pre><code>//In the Security Provider script, after the groups of the user are set
user.CheckMcpCall = (tool) => CountMcpCallsToday(user.WebUserName) &gt;= 500 ? "The limit of 500 calls per day is reached." : null;
user.OnMcpCall = (tool, isError) => AddMcpCall(user.WebUserName);
user.GetAICostLimit = () => 20 - GetAICostOfMonth(user.WebUserName);
user.OnAIUsage = (usage, cost) => AddAICost(user.WebUserName, cost ?? 0);</code></pre>
                            <div class="bs-callout bs-callout-warning">
                                <ck>Check <a href="~/Server#lineSecurity_group">Security Groups</a> for the rights configuration</ck>.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- end col -->
                    </div>
                    <!-- end row -->
                </section>
                <!-- end section -->
                <section id="lineMcp" class="section">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12 left-align">
                            <h2 class="dark-text">MCP Server <hr></h2>
                        </div>
                        <!-- end col -->
                    </div>
                    <!-- end row -->
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12">
                            <p>
                                The <b>Web Report Server</b> can also serve the AI agents to <strong>external AI clients</strong> (<eg>e.g. Claude Code, Claude Desktop, VS Code Copilot, Cursor</eg>) with the <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank">Model Context Protocol</a>.<br />
                                The client uses <b>its own AI model</b>: the provider of the agent is not used. The tools are executed by the server <b>with the rights of the user</b>, exactly as in the chat panel.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <strong>Enabling the MCP server</strong>
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Run the <b>Server Manager</b>, select <srmenu>Configuration->Configure AI...</srmenu> and set <code>MCP server enabled</code> (<i>Danger Zone</i>, disabled by default).</li>
                                <li>The <code>Channel</code> of each agent defines where it is served: <i>Web</i> (chat panel only), <i>MCP</i> or <i>Web and MCP</i> (default). Set <i>Web</i> for an agent whose data must not leave its own provider.</li>
                                <li>An agent is published at <code>https://&lt;server&gt;/mcp/&lt;agent&gt;</code>, the agent being its name in lower case with the other characters replaced by '-' (<eg>e.g. <code>/mcp/report-designer</code>, <code>/mcp/data-analyst</code></eg>). A user only reaches the agents assigned to his security groups.</li>
                                <li>The limits of the <i>MCP Server</i> category: <code>MCP token maximum validity</code> (365 days), <code>MCP token maximum inactivity</code> (no limit) and <code>MCP maximum calls per minute</code> per user (60).</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p>
                                <strong>Connecting a client</strong>
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>In the Web Report Server, open the user profile, tab <b>MCP access</b> (shown only if the user has MCP agents): create a <b>personal access token</b> with a name and a validity, and copy it: it is displayed only once. The tab also lists the MCP URLs of the agents of the user.</li>
                                <li>Declare the server in the client with the URL of the agent and the header <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code>. With Claude Code:</li>
                            </ul>
                            <pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http seal-designer https://&lt;server&gt;/mcp/report-designer --header "Authorization: Bearer seal_mcp_..."</code></pre>
                            <p>
                                <strong>Connecting a client with OAuth (claude.ai, Claude Desktop, Claude Code...)</strong>
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Set <code>MCP OAuth enabled</code> (<i>Danger Zone</i>, disabled by default): the MCP server is then also an <b>OAuth 2.1 authorization server</b> and a client connects to an agent with its URL only, without token to copy.</li>
                                <li>In the client, add the URL of the agent as a connector (<eg>e.g. claude.ai or Claude Desktop: <i>Settings > Connectors > Add custom connector</i>; Claude Code: <code>claude mcp add --transport http seal-designer https://&lt;server&gt;/mcp/report-designer</code> then <code>/mcp</code> to authenticate</eg>).</li>
                                <li>The browser opens the authorization page of the Web Report Server: the user logs in (password, Two-Factor Authentication or single sign-on), checks the client, the address it is redirected to and the tools of the agent, then authorizes it. The client receives an access token valid for this agent only, renewed with a refresh token.</li>
                                <li>The authorizations are listed in the profile, tab <b>MCP access</b>, section <i>Authorized applications</i>, where they can be revoked.</li>
                                <li>Settings of the <i>MCP Server</i> category: <code>MCP public URL</code> (the URL the users enter in their client, required behind a proxy), <code>MCP OAuth redirect URIs</code> (clients allowed, by default Claude: <code>https://claude.ai/api/mcp/auth_callback</code>, <code>https://claude.com/api/mcp/auth_callback</code> and the loopback addresses of Claude Code), <code>MCP OAuth dynamic client registration</code>, <code>MCP OAuth access token validity</code> (60 minutes), <code>MCP OAuth authorization maximum duration</code> (30 days, the user must then log in again) and <code>MCP OAuth requires a strong login</code> (Two-Factor Authentication or single sign-on).</li>
                                <li>Standards: discovery by the protected resource metadata (RFC 9728) and the authorization server metadata (RFC 8414, also at <code>/.well-known/openid-configuration</code>), clients identified by a Client ID Metadata Document or registered dynamically (RFC 7591), PKCE S256 required, tokens bound to the agent (RFC 8707), rotation of the refresh tokens with revocation of the authorization if a token is reused, revocation endpoint (RFC 7009).</li>
                                <li>The server must be served in HTTPS and, for claude.ai and Claude Desktop, be reachable from the Internet (Anthropic addresses <code>160.79.104.0/21</code>). If the Web Report Server is in a virtual directory (<eg>e.g. <code>https://&lt;server&gt;/seal</code></eg>), the clients find the authorization server with the header <code>WWW-Authenticate</code> of the MCP server and with <code>/seal/.well-known/openid-configuration</code>.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p>
                                The instructions sent to the client are the system prompt of the agent. All the tools of the agent and of its skills are listed upfront: a tool belonging to a skill is described as <i>Requires the skill ...</i> and the client calls <code>load_skill</code> before using it.
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><b>Tool annotations</b>: the <code>Access</code> property of each tool (<i>Read only</i>, <i>Write</i> or <i>Destructive</i>) is published as MCP tool annotations, so that the client can ask a confirmation before the tools that write or delete.</li>
                                <li><b>Prompts</b>: the sample prompts of the agent, translated in the user language, are published as MCP prompts (<eg>e.g. the slash commands of Claude Code</eg>).</li>
                                <li><b>Resources</b>: the reports of the user folders (<code>seal://report/Reports/...</code>, 500 at most) and the data sources he can access (<code>seal://source/&lt;name&gt;</code>) can be attached to a conversation (<eg>e.g. with @@ in Claude Code</eg>). Reading a resource executes the tool <code>report_get_detail</code> or <code>datasource_get_detail</code> of the agent: it is published only if the agent has this tool.</li>
                                <li><b>Progress</b>: when the client requests it, the progress text of a tool is notified at its start, then every 5 seconds until the end of a long execution.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p>
                                <strong>Security and monitoring</strong>
                            </p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Each request is authenticated on its own: the user of the token is loaded again by the Security Provider, so a change of his groups or rights applies immediately.
                                    The provider is then executed from the user name only, without password and without Two-Factor Authentication (<code>user.ForSchedule</code> is true): it must support this mode, check <a href="~/Server#lineSecurity_provider_name_only">Authentication from the user name only</a> (<eg>e.g. the service account of the LDAP and Database providers</eg>).</li>
                                <li>The login on the OAuth authorization page is the login of the Web Report Server (Security Provider with password, Two-Factor Authentication or single sign-on). The user must have a name (<code>user.WebUserName</code>): an anonymous access cannot authorize a client.</li>
                                <li>Only the SHA-256 hash of a token is stored (<i>/Security/McpTokens</i>, the OAuth clients and authorizations in its sub-folders). A token or an authorization is revoked from the profile; an expired or inactive token is refused.</li>
                                <li>Every tool call, error and refusal is written in the audit (types <code>AIMcpCall</code>, <code>AIMcpCallError</code>, <code>AIMcpRefused</code>, and <code>AIMcpAuthorization</code> for the OAuth authorizations given, refused or revoked) with the IP address and the application of the client. The System report <i>270 Audit - MCP Activity</i> shows the activity per day, user and tool, the errors and the inventory of the tokens and OAuth authorizations of all the users.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <!-- end col -->
                    </div>
                    <!-- end row -->
                </section>
                <!-- end section -->
                <section id="lineSemantic" class="section">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12 left-align">
